{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121322","id":4044130502,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7xDIjG","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121322","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121322.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121322.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121322","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121322/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121322/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121322/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/3f32c9ace912849ad253cffb37f1f4ed7e92603b","number":121322,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"GDScript: Check for soft function return types in various places","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nThe following code would previously not compile even though the getter is untyped:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar _prop: int\r\nvar prop: String: get = get_f\r\n\r\nfunc get_f():\r\n    return _prop\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt now passes the analyzer. (Note: I think we have an issue with untyped getters were we are missing runtime checks somewhere, but that's nothing related to this change as the same also occurs with explicitly typing `get_f() -> Variant` which the analyzer already allows).\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe following code would give wrong return type hints in the editor:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar _prop: int\r\n\r\nfunc get_f():\r\n    return _prop\r\n\r\nfunc test():\r\n    get_f()\r\n```\r\n\r\n<img width=\"265\" height=\"235\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a4c13435-611c-4fec-9b3f-c5a4e42739ce\" />\r\n\r\nIt now correctly shows the actual type of the function:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"265\" height=\"235\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cbe2c635-ee8e-4b62-b64e-5e17c7394ed1\" />\r\n\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nEspecially the first issue might seem like a non-issue when viewed in isolation. However when looking at the analyzer as a whole it is one of the few cases, where soft-types do have an actual effect on something compilation critical. So we need to get rid of that behaviour if we want to remove soft-types.\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.co